 "summaries": [
  {
   "section": "Tires",
   "text": "The vehicle is equipped with correctly sized tires, and all four tires have an adequate amount of remaining tread depth. The tires are Goodyear tires. Three of the tires shows gouges. The wheels shows scratches and curb rash."
  },
  {
   "section": "Exterior",
   "text": "The wipers are worn and should be replaced. There are minor misc scratches around the vehicle. Normal for mileage and most too small to see in photos. There is one minor ding on the tailgate. The paint shows some wear and tear that is consistent with age and mileage. The sunroof only achieves the vent position and gets jammed when commanded to open, Further diagnosis is needed. Window trim and door seals were sound. Glass was free of obvious damage. Headlights and tail lights were clear and free of obvious cracks or other damage."
  },
  {
   "section": "Interior",
   "text": "The steering wheel shows wear. There is light wear to the seats. Normal for mileage. The inner door panels show wear consistent with age and mileage. The interior trim shows normal wear consistent with age and mileage. There's scratches on some parts of interior trim. The TPMS warning light is illuminated, Further diagnosis is needed. The carpet shows normal wear consistent with age and mileage. The sunglass compartment was broken when the client had the windshield replaced. There were no indications of smoke or unusual odors. The climate control and infotainment systems were observed to function properly. The windows, locks, mirrors, and gauges operated properly during the inspection."
  },
  {
   "section": "Mechanical",
   "text": "The engine coolant level is low, with no obvious external coolant leaks the system should be topped off and pressure tested for internal or external leaks. Exhaust shows some surface rust, but at this time has no leaks and sounds good. Inspection under the oil fill cap found no signs of excessive moisture or sludge accumulation. Hoses and belts appeared to be sound. No fluid leaks were noted from the engine's top or bottom or the transmission's bottom. Inspection underneath the vehicle found all splash guards and protective panels in place."
  },
  {
   "section": "Road Test",
   "text": "There is a growling noise while driving that is suspiciously similar to a bearing growl. The tires are admittedly loud, but the tire noise is notably different, Further diagnosis is needed. The TPMS light is on, Further diagnosis is needed. I hooked up my Scan Tool to the computer system and found several codes across multiple systems. See pictures of more descriptive information. More diagnoses are needed. The transmission functioned properly as designed, and the vehicle handled and braked well."
  }
 ],
